// The sprites of the Ink skin, cut out of Generic Dark Pixel UI by Flatus (flatus.itch.io/generic-dark-pixel-ui, CC0)
// with the frame of Fantasy UI Borders by Kenney (kenney.nl, opengameart.org/content/fantasy-ui-borders, CC0) by
// Art/make_ui_packs.py, which is where to change anything in here, this file is written by it. Flatus's pack is one
// sheet of dark greys about thirteen pixels a piece, with panels that are see-through in the middle, which is the point
// of this skin, Fighter2D's menus over a live map that you can still see. The one ornate thing is Kenney's fret, a
// lattice border in gold that a screen puts round the one box that matters (the frame sprite). Kenney's art is drawn
// two pixels to the pixel, it is halved here so its lines are as thin as everything else.
//
// Night is the greys pulled over to the indigo of the Japan map after dark, ink is the pack as it comes. Either way
// the selected thing has a ring of sakura pink round it.
//
// The names are the ones the components and the layouts ask for, which are Dead Revolver's, so a layout written
// for that skin comes up in this one.

